{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>And Irad begot.</b> There are places where it says הוֹלִיד [in the hif'il] and places where it says יָלַד, for the root of לֵדָה serves in two senses: the giving birth of the woman — ניש\"טרא בְּלַעַ\"ז — and the begetting of offspring by the man — אינזי\"ראר בְּלַעַ\"ז. When it says הוֹלִיד in the hif'il conjugation, it speaks of the woman's giving birth — So-and-so's wife bore him a son or a daughter. When it says יָלַד, it speaks of the man's begetting."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {0 "the la'az ניש\"טרא is Old French enfanter, 'to give birth'; אינזי\"ראר is Old French engendrer, 'to beget'"}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:57:34.155094516Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}